---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The MIT licence above covers everything shipped in this mod, with no carve-out.
That is not the usual case in this repository, so it is worth saying why it
holds here: this mod redistributes nothing. No code, no defs, no textures, no
sounds from any other mod are included.

What ships is:

  - Source/WorkGivers.cs, two classes each overriding one property, written
    against Dubs Bad Hygiene's public API rather than copied from it
  - Source/ManureCompostingDefs.cs, a lazy def lookup
  - the def files and the three patch files, written against the current 1.6
    defs of each target
  - Source/Building_ManureComposter.cs, an original text-only adapter
  - original translation resources and generated artwork
  - the packaging and the documentation

THE MODS IT DEPENDS ON ARE NOT INCLUDED IN IT. Dubs Bad Hygiene supplies
Building_Composter, CompProperties_Composter, the composter jobs, the
Biosolids item and the composter texture; Burok's Manure supplies the Manure
and DryManure items and the whole simulation behind them. Both are hard
dependencies, loaded at runtime from the player's own copy. The composter here
is a def that points at DBH's class and at DBH's texture path - it is DBH's
code running on our def, not a copy of DBH.

VELCROBOY'S MANURE IS ACKNOWLEDGED, NOT PORTED.

  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3252954927

That mod (1.3 and 1.5, last updated 2025-01-18) is where the idea of a manure
composter and the list of integrations worth having came from, and it is
credited for that in the About and in ATTRIBUTION.md. None of its code, defs,
textures or strings are here, so its own undeclared licence, and the fact that
its Credit.txt says most of its code came from Dubs Bad Hygiene, do not reach
this mod.

If Burok or Dubwise would rather this mod did not exist against theirs, say so
and it comes down. Immediately, and without discussion.

ATTRIBUTION.md records what each dependency supplies and what was written here.
